t and the other group off from new material as it comes in, breaking contin=
uity. It tends moreover to tick off more experienced speakers, who have lea=
rned the older form and are now asked to relearn (which is very hard =E2=80=
=93 I still, nearly 40 later, am most likely to come up with a Loglan word =
as my first attempt). And, alas, all this tends to create internal tensions=
, which can tear a constructed-language community apart, resulting, typical=
